  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Using <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>at</mi><mo>&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo><mi>or</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>at</mi><mo>,</mo></math> we find that if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>→</mo></mover></mfenced></math> is doubled,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></math>&nbsp;will be halved.<br /><br />If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></math> is the time for accelerations, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> is the time for retardation.<br /><br />Now, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p>"
